 ## Background
-The method was introduced in "Automating Transfer Function Design for Volume Rendering Using Hierarchical Clustering of Material Boundaries" (EuroVis 2006) [S1]. It was demonstrated on CT datasets of an engine and a carp [S1]. The approach was designed to work with the VolumePro1000 rendering board, which imposes 1D TF constraints, necessitating the label-based approach [S1].
+Originated in the paper "Automating Transfer Function Design for Volume Rendering Using Hierarchical Clustering of Material Boundaries" (EuroVis 2006) [S1]. The method builds on the concept of hierarchical clustering in LH space to automate TF design [S1]. It is used in volume rendering to simplify the process of defining color and opacity mappings for complex datasets [S1].
 
